Overlay patch 0054 (VR R17 part B): THE ALT-ASSETS SWITCH SAYS SO.

WHAT HAPPENED. the user reported the 4K texture pack "not loading" on 1.0.1.21.
It loads: the pack (21.77 GB) mounts on every boot, HD textures were live for the
first five minutes of the session, and they stopped mid-session at ~13:10:28. The
headset's Documents/shipofharkinian.json then read

    "gSettings.AltAssets": 0

which is SoH's own "Enable Mods" switch, off. Nothing in this port's VR layer can
write it: the only two writers in the whole tree are the ImGui checkbox
(soh/soh/Enhancements/mod_menu.cpp, RegisterModMenuWidgets) and the Tab hotkey
(OTRGlobals.cpp's LUS_KB_TAB case), and no VR control synthesises a Tab. Overlay
0053 is proven innocent by the logs themselves: ZERO "clamping oversized texture"
lines across every 1.0.1.21 log, against 138 in 1.0.1.20.

the user re-enables the switch himself. This patch is about the NEXT time, and it
does exactly two things.

(a) THE STATE CHANGE IS LOUD. OTRGlobals.cpp's per-frame CVar sync is the one
    place in the program that observes the switch actually moving --

        bool curAltAssets = CVarGetInteger(CVAR_SETTING("AltAssets"), 1);
        if (prevAltAssets != curAltAssets) { ... SetAltAssetsEnabled(cur) ... }

    -- and it said nothing at all, which is why "the pack stopped loading" and
    "somebody turned mods off" were indistinguishable for a day. It now writes
    one line into Documents/vr-mem.log through the shell's SohIos_VrNote, beside
    the heartbeat and the audio notes, so a later pull carries the MOMENT the
    switch moved in the same timestamp order as everything else. spdlog gets the
    line too, at error level, because that file is what a desktop user would
    send.

(b) THE TAB HOTKEY DEFAULTS OFF ON iOS. `Mods.AlternateAssetsHotkey` defaults to
    TRUE upstream, which is right on a desktop with a real keyboard and wrong on
    a platform where the only Tab that can arrive is a forged one. This port has
    already shipped one bug of exactly that shape: iPadOS forges a keyboard
    Escape from a controller's B button (SohIosShell.m's input-trace note), and
    SDL's UIKit backend delivered it as SDL_SCANCODE_ESCAPE with no controller
    binding anywhere in the path to stop it. A forged Tab would toggle a 21.77 GB
    asset pack with no UI feedback whatsoever. Both the READER's default and the
    checkbox's DefaultValue move together, because a widget that shows "on" while
    the reader defaults to off is a worse state than either.

    This does NOT disable the switch, the pack, or the menu checkbox. the user can
    still turn the hotkey on in the Mod Menu, and turning mods on and off from
    the checkbox is untouched.

Both edits are __IOS__-only: the macOS build and every desktop build compile
byte-for-byte vanilla.

--- a/soh/soh/OTRGlobals.cpp
+++ b/soh/soh/OTRGlobals.cpp
@@ -155,6 +155,13 @@
 
 bool prevAltAssets = false;
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+// R17 part B item 3: one line into Documents/vr-mem.log when the alt-assets
+// ("Enable Mods") switch moves. Defined in app/ios/SohIosShell.m, which no
+// desktop build links -- hence the guard.
+extern "C" void SohIos_VrNote(const char* what, const char* detail);
+#endif
+
 // Same as NaviColor type from OoT src (z_actor.c), but modified to be sans alpha channel for Controller LED.
 typedef struct {
     Color_RGB8 inner;
@@ -1755,7 +1762,17 @@
         }
 #endif
         case KbScancode::LUS_KB_TAB: {
+#ifdef __IOS__
+            // R17 part B item 3(b): DEFAULT OFF on iOS. The only Tab that can
+            // reach here is a forged one -- iPadOS already forges a keyboard
+            // Escape out of a controller's B button on this platform, with no
+            // controller binding anywhere in the path to stop it -- and a
+            // forged Tab silently toggles a 21.77 GB asset pack. the user can
+            // still switch the hotkey on in the Mod Menu.
+            if (CVarGetInteger(CVAR_SETTING("Mods.AlternateAssetsHotkey"), 0)) {
+#else
             if (CVarGetInteger(CVAR_SETTING("Mods.AlternateAssetsHotkey"), 1)) {
+#endif
                 CVarSetInteger(CVAR_SETTING("AltAssets"), !CVarGetInteger(CVAR_SETTING("AltAssets"), 1));
             }
             break;
@@ -1844,6 +1861,15 @@
     bool curAltAssets = CVarGetInteger(CVAR_SETTING("AltAssets"), 1);
     if (prevAltAssets != curAltAssets) {
         prevAltAssets = curAltAssets;
+#ifdef __IOS__
+        // R17 part B item 3(a): THE ONLY PLACE THE SWITCH IS SEEN TO MOVE.
+        // It said nothing, so "the 4K pack stopped loading" and "mods got
+        // turned off" were indistinguishable for a day. One line, in the
+        // same file and the same timestamp order as the heartbeat.
+        SPDLOG_ERROR("SOH_IOS: alternate assets (Enable Mods) -> {}", curAltAssets ? "ON" : "OFF");
+        SohIos_VrNote("alt assets", curAltAssets ? "ENABLED (mods and texture packs live)"
+                                                : "DISABLED (vanilla assets) -- gSettings.AltAssets is 0");
+#endif
         Ship::Context::GetRawInstance()->GetResourceManager()->SetAltAssetsEnabled(curAltAssets);
         gfx_texture_cache_clear();
         SOH::SkeletonPatcher::UpdateSkeletons();
--- a/soh/soh/Enhancements/mod_menu.cpp
+++ b/soh/soh/Enhancements/mod_menu.cpp
@@ -537,10 +537,21 @@
     tabHotkeyWidget = { .name = "Mods Tab Hotkey", .type = WidgetType::WIDGET_CVAR_CHECKBOX };
     tabHotkeyWidget.CVar(CVAR_SETTING("Mods.AlternateAssetsHotkey"))
         .RaceDisable(false)
+#ifdef __IOS__
+        // R17 part B item 3(b): the checkbox and the reader in OTRGlobals.cpp
+        // must default the same way, or the menu shows "on" for a hotkey that
+        // is off. There is no Tab key on this platform to press deliberately.
         .Options(UIWidgets::CheckboxOptions()
                      .Color(THEME_COLOR)
+                     .Tooltip("Allows pressing the Tab key to toggle mods (off by default on iOS: "
+                              "the only Tab that can arrive here is a forged one)")
+                     .DefaultValue(false));
+#else
+        .Options(UIWidgets::CheckboxOptions()
+                     .Color(THEME_COLOR)
                      .Tooltip("Allows pressing the Tab key to toggle mods")
                      .DefaultValue(true));
+#endif
     SohGui::mSohMenu->AddSearchWidget(
         { tabHotkeyWidget, "Settings", "Mod Menu", "Top", "alternate assets tab hotkey" });
 }
